        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(android): make gateway QR pairing prominent in Settings",
        "body": "Closes #106186\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where pairing an Android phone with a gateway — the first-run action for every new device — was noisier and less discoverable than on iOS. Settings → Gateway had two identical \"Add gateway\" buttons in adjacent panels, buried setup-code entry inside a combined \"Connection Setup\" panel with always-expanded token/bootstrap/password fields, never showed discovered gateways (discovery already runs), and offered no nav-bar scan entry or first-run call to action.\n\nAndroid follow-up to the iOS restructure (#106013 / #106111).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`GatewaySettingsScreen` now mirrors the iOS ordering and entry points:\n\n- **Nav-bar QR scan button** — `SettingsDetailFrame` gains an optional `trailingAction` slot; the Gateway screen puts a `QrCode2` scan button next to the title.\n- **First-run hero** — a prominent \"Scan QR to Pair\" button shows while no gateway is paired (`gatewayShowsScanHero`).\n- **Facts parity** — the metric panel adds Discovered / Default Agent / Agents / Instance ID rows (all data already on the ViewModel).\n- **Diagnose** — copies the existing gateway diagnostics report (same helper chat uses).\n- **Add Gateway panel** — one pairing panel owns Scan QR, setup-code paste + Connect, the \"where do I get a code\" help text, and a **discovered gateways list** with per-row Connect (`viewModel.connect(endpoint)`); discovery starts on screen entry like onboarding.\n- **Manual Gateway panel** — host/port/TLS and credential fields move to the bottom as plumbing; its Save & Connect is now manual-only (setup code lives in Add Gateway).\n- **Screenshot harness** — new `gateway` scene (`AndroidScreenshotScene.Gateway` → Settings tab + Gateway route) so this screen finally has deterministic capture; `scripts/android-screenshots.sh` captures it.\n\nNew strings ran the full native i18n pipeline (inventory, 21-locale translation, Android `strings.xml` + `NativeStringResources` projection). The discovered-row `host:port` subtitle is a format-only literal and is allowlisted in `android-app-i18n.ts` per existing convention (`$versionName-dev`, `> $line`).\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users pairing a new gateway see Scan QR immediately — in the nav bar, as a hero while unpaired, and first in the Add Gateway panel — and can now tap nearby discovered gateways to connect directly. Manual/credential plumbing is out of the way but unchanged in behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Before → After** (emulator, deterministic screenshot fixture):\n\n| Before (top) | After (top) | After (Add Gateway) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ![before-top](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/2026-07-android-gateway-qr/before-gateway-top.png) | ![after-top](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/2026-07-android-gateway-qr/after-gateway-top.png) | ![after-mid](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/2026-07-android-gateway-qr/after-gateway-mid.png) |\n\nOld layout for reference: [before-mid](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/2026-07-android-gateway-qr/before-gateway-mid.png) (duplicate Add gateway buttons, combined Connection Setup). Full bottom of new screen: [after-bottom](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/2026-07-android-gateway-qr/after-gateway-bottom.png).\n\n- `:app:compilePlayDebugKotlin`, `:app:ktlintCheck`: green.\n- Focused JVM tests green: `SettingsScreensTest` (new `gatewayShowsScanHero` / `gatewayDiscoveredRowSubtitle` cases + a source-order guard for the pairing-first layout), `AndroidScreenshotModeTest` (gateway scene mapping), `GatewayConfigResolverTest`.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/android-app-i18n.test.ts`: pass.\n- `native-app-i18n check`, `android-app-i18n check`, `apple-app-i18n check`: all pass.\n- Gateway scene verified on emulator via `--es openclaw.screenshotScene gateway` (screenshots above); `oxfmt`/`oxlint` clean on the touched script.\n",
        "branch": "claude/android-gateway-qr-parity",
